      "textEn": "Their bodies became as cold as ice. Hey Rajan! While grieving, he remembered the teachings of Rishi Angira.\nAnd he renounced the desire to have a son. According to the instructions of the Brahmins, she went to the banks of the Yamuna, bathed there, and for her sins,\nshe atoned. Note: The word Bala-hatya-hata-prabhaah is specifically mentioned in this verse. The practice of infanticide has been going on in human society for a long time, but at that time it was rarely\ndone. But now, in the age of Kali, abortion—the killing of the fetus—has become commonplace. Even sometimes after birth, the child is murdered. If a woman does such\nheinous act, she slowly loses the radiance of her body. (BAR-KAY-LAH-TOO-BAR-KAY-LAH-TOO-BAR). Here, it is also important to note that the women who had committed the heinous sin of poisoning the child,\nwere extremely ashamed and had to atone for the infanticide according to the orders of the Brahmins.\nIf a woman has ever committed such a misdeed, then she has to atone, but\nNowadays, no one does that. In such a state, the woman who is the culprit of infanticide will have to suffer in this\nlife and in the next birth. Hearing this incident, truthful souls\nshould abstain from infanticide and seriously devote themselves to Lord Krishna for their misdeeds.\nShould do. If someone chants the Hare Krishna Mahamantra with innocence, then immediately his\nall sins are atoned for, but man should not repeat such deeds, because\nthis is a sin. S Ittham pratibuddhatma chitraketur dwijoktibhih. The one who has crossed the wells of the house, the one who has crossed the river like a boat. 15. Lexicon"
